  "_comment": "Manifest of every src/app/api/**/route.ts handler in cfw-social. The `auth` tag is the GATEWAY-level auth (what src/proxy.ts allows), NOT just what the handler imports. Many handlers call requireApiBrand but the middleware blocks unauthenticated traffic upstream, so the effective auth is `session`. Placeholders inside {...} must match a key in PLACEHOLDER inside smoke.mjs. SMOKE-SAFETY: api-or-session routes are called WITH master-key headers — data-creating routes (agents, api-keys, posts/quick, brand-secrets PUT) deliberately carry INVALID bodies so they 400 instead of creating/overwriting real rows. A doc-oriented sibling copy (realistic bodies) lives in the c-cfw-social skill — keep auth tags in sync. Regenerate by hand; bump _version.",
